# Live scheduler state. These are written by a running cron process, not by a
# person: a SQLite ledger with its WAL sidecars, the two dispatch locks, and the
# ticker's liveness stamps. They showed up in a fleet cleanup pass as 7 untracked
# files planned for `:additive` landing -- the class whose argument is "no such
# path exists on the default branch, so nothing is rewritten". True, and still
# wrong: they are this machine's runtime, not work.
executions.db
executions.db-shm
executions.db-wal
.jobs.lock
.tick.lock
ticker_heartbeat
ticker_last_success
.nbb/
